---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

// Plain-language privacy policy. Every statement here describes how the site
// actually runs; when the deployment changes (deploy/, the Caddyfile, a new
// third-party service), this page changes with it. The effective date is the
// date of the last substantive edit.
const EFFECTIVE = "November 7, 2026";
---

<Base
	title="Privacy — Chino Valley Today"
	description="What Chino Valley Today collects about readers (almost nothing), what our hosting providers see, and how to reach us."
>
	<header class="legalhead">
		<div class="shell legalhead__inner">
			<h1 class="legalhead__title">Privacy</h1>
			<p class="legalhead__date mark">Effective {EFFECTIVE}</p>
		</div>
	</header>

	<div class="reading body prose">
		<p>
			Chino Valley Today is a local news site about Chino and Chino Hills. It
			is built to be read, not to watch its readers. This page says what is
			collected, by whom, and why.
		</p>

		<h2>The short version</h2>
		<ul>
			<li>No accounts, no sign-up, no newsletter list.</li>
			<li>No analytics, advertising, or tracking scripts, and no cookies of our own.</li>
			<li>
				Our web server keeps a short-lived technical log of requests, as every
				web server does.
			</li>
			<li>If you email us, we have your email.</li>
			<li>We do not sell or share personal information.</li>
		</ul>

		<h2>When you read the site</h2>
		<p>
			Pages are plain HTML. Nearly every page ships no script at all, and the
			fonts are served from our own server, so reading a page contacts no one
			but us and our network provider.
		</p>
		<p>
			<strong>Server logs.</strong> Our web server records each request: the
			IP address it came from, the page, the time, and what your browser
			reports about itself (its user agent). We use these logs only to keep
			the site running and to investigate abuse, and they are kept for no more
			than 30 days.
		</p>
		<p>
			<strong>Cloudflare.</strong> Traffic reaches us through Cloudflare, which
			provides the site's encryption and protects it from attacks. Cloudflare
			processes the same request information to do that, and may set a
			strictly necessary security cookie. Its handling is described in the
			<a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" rel="noopener noreferrer"
				>Cloudflare privacy policy</a
			>.
		</p>
		<p>
			<strong>Feeds and the podcast.</strong> The RSS feed and podcast episodes
			are ordinary files on the same server, and requests for them are logged
			the same way. Your feed reader or podcast app has its own privacy
			practices.
		</p>

		<h2>When you email us</h2>
		<p>
			Mail to <a href="mailto:corrections@chinovalley.today"
				>corrections@chinovalley.today</a
			> is forwarded to the editor by Cloudflare Email Routing. We use your
			message and address to answer you and to make any correction you report.
			We do not add you to any list, and we do not publish your name or message
			without asking.
		</p>

		<h2>Third-party content you choose to play</h2>
		<p>
			Some pages may feature a video hosted by a social platform, such as
			TikTok. Nothing from that platform loads until you press play. When you
			do, the video plays in the platform's own player, and the platform's
			privacy policy applies to that player, including any cookies it sets.
			Links that leave this site are governed by the site they lead to.
		</p>

		<h2>People named in the record</h2>
		<p>
			The site reports from public records: agendas, minutes, meeting video,
			licence reports, and agency releases. Those records sometimes name
			people. Our editorial rules limit when a private individual is named and
			never name minors; see <a href="/about/">About</a>. To ask about an item
			that names you, email the address above.
		</p>

		<h2>Children</h2>
		<p>
			The site is not directed at children and collects no information from
			them.
		</p>

		<h2>Your choices and rights</h2>
		<p>
			You can read everything here without giving us anything. If you have
			emailed us and want that correspondence deleted, or want to know what we
			hold about you, email the address above and we will answer within 30
			days. California residents have rights under the California Consumer
			Privacy Act; we honor requests made under it, although we do not sell or
			share personal information as that law defines those terms.
		</p>

		<h2>Changes</h2>
		<p>
			When this policy changes, the effective date at the top changes with it.
			A change that collects more about readers will be explained on this page
			before it takes effect.
		</p>
	</div>
</Base>

<style>
	.legalhead {
		background: var(--crate);
		color: #fff;
		border-bottom: 6px solid var(--placard);
	}
	.legalhead__inner {
		padding-block: 1.9rem 2.2rem;
		max-width: 44rem;
	}
	.legalhead__title {
		margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
		font-size: clamp(1.55rem, 1.2rem + 2vw, 2.5rem);
		line-height: 1.16;
		font-weight: 600;
	}
	.legalhead__date {
		margin: 0;
		font-size: 0.78rem;
	}
	.body {
		padding-block: 2.4rem 1rem;
	}
</style>
